WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.420
Secure configuration management starts with inventory and classification.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.760
Identify configuration sources, owners, and environments.

3
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.260
Classify values by sensitivity and risk.

4
00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:16.400
Separate configuration from secrets and handle each according to its requirements.

5
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.500
Keep real .env files and production secrets out of source control.

6
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:28.600
Use .env.example or documented variable lists to make expected configuration visible without exposing real values.

7
00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.160
Validate early and choose safe defaults.

8
00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:38.020
Validate configuration at startup and fail closed for unsafe security-critical values.

9
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:54.920
Review CORS, cookies, authentication, TLS, proxy trust, logging, rate limits, upload limits, request size limits, feature flags, debug behavior, and error handling as configuration-driven security controls.

10
00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:58.540
Do not let development defaults silently carry into production.

11
00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:04.240
Do not treat NODE_ENV or any single environment name as a complete security control.

12
00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.760
Protect delivery and operations.

13
00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:10.540
Separate development, test, staging, and production values.

14
00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.800
Protect CI/CD and deployment configuration with least privilege and approval.

15
00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:20.100
Govern feature flags and remote configuration when they affect security behavior.

16
00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:28.520
Detect drift, redact logs, monitor important changes, and include configuration in incident response.

17
00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.940
Configuration changes should be reviewed, recoverable, and observable.

18
00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:55.220
A practical first-week plan is direct: inventory environment variables, create or update .env.example, add configuration schema validation, remove production secrets from local workflows, review CORS and cookie settings, confirm production debug behavior is disabled, document feature flag owners, and add redaction for configuration-related logs.

19
00:01:55.320 --> 00:02:01.960
The long-term goal is a repeatable workflow where configuration changes are as deliberate as code changes.
